# Labeled eval set for the baseline harness. Reuses the questions + qids from
# financial_qa.jsonl and adds retrieval labels. Two row kinds via `route`:
#
#   route="filing" (default): a SEC-filing retrieval question. `expected_sources`
#     are distinctive, answer-bearing anchor phrases the relevant passage should
#     contain. Because document_chunks are character-split with no durable id, an
#     anchor phrase IS the source identifier: a retrieved chunk is relevant to a
#     source if its text contains that phrase (case-insensitive). `filing_type`
#     (10-K / 10-Q) is the stable filing identifier the harness filters on. These
#     rows are scored (hit@k / recall@k / MRR).
#
#   route="live": a market-data / live question answered from Yahoo Finance (and,
#     for trends, SEC EDGAR XBRL company-facts) — there is NO filing to retrieve,
#     so retrieval_eval SKIPS these from scoring and only records their expected
#     data source. They exist to document market-data use-case coverage.
#
# `category` groups by use case. Anchors are a first pass — the harness prints
# which matched; tune against the actual ingested filing. All rows are AAPL.
